{#
  treatment.j2 — evidence-based treatment generation.
  Forces the AI to use RAG-retrieved knowledge base content.
  Category-constrained with Uganda/East Africa context.
#}

Generate specific, evidence-based treatment recommendations for a {{ plant_identified }} farmer.

DIAGNOSIS:
- Plant:    {{ plant_identified }}
- Disease:  {{ diagnosis.name if diagnosis else "Unknown" }}
- Category: {{ disease_category | default("unknown") }}
- Severity: {{ diagnosis.severity if diagnosis else "unknown" }}
- Description: {{ diagnosis.description if diagnosis else "" }}

{% if retrieved_context %}
━━ KNOWLEDGE BASE — YOU MUST USE THIS INFORMATION ━━
The following is verified information from authoritative agricultural PDFs.
Base your treatment recommendations DIRECTLY on this content.
Quote specific products, rates, and timings mentioned in these sources.
Do NOT ignore this information — it must shape your recommendations.

{% for chunk in retrieved_context %}
━━ Source: {{ chunk.document_name }} (Relevance: {{ "%.0f"|format(chunk.similarity_score * 100) }}%) ━━
{{ chunk.chunk_text }}

{% endfor %}
━━ END KNOWLEDGE BASE ━━
{% else %}
⚠ No knowledge base content retrieved. Use your training knowledge about
{{ diagnosis.name if diagnosis else "this disease" }} on {{ plant_identified }} in East Africa.
{% endif %}

{% if weather_data %}
Current field conditions (factor these into timing recommendations):
- Temperature: {{ weather_data.temperature }}°C
- Humidity: {{ weather_data.humidity }}%
{% if weather_data.humidity > 80 %}
⚠ HIGH HUMIDITY — prioritise reducing leaf wetness. Recommend early morning application.
{% endif %}
{% if weather_data.temperature > 35 %}
⚠ HIGH TEMPERATURE — recommend applying treatments at dawn or dusk only.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% if differential_diagnoses and differential_diagnoses|length > 1 %}
Also monitor for these alternative conditions:
{% for d in differential_diagnoses[1:] %}
- {{ d.name }} ({{ d.probability }}% probability) — {{ d.category }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

━━ STRICT TREATMENT RULES ━━

{% if disease_category == "fungal" %}
FUNGAL DISEASE:
✓ Recommend specific fungicide active ingredients mentioned in the knowledge base above
✓ Include application frequency and timing from the knowledge base
✓ Remove and destroy infected leaves — bag and burn, never compost
✓ Improve air circulation through pruning or adjusted plant spacing
✓ Rotate fungicide groups to prevent resistance development
✗ DO NOT recommend bactericides

{% elif disease_category == "bacterial" %}
BACTERIAL DISEASE:
✓ Copper-based bactericide (copper hydroxide or copper oxychloride) — apply per label
✓ Remove and destroy ALL infected material — do not compost
✓ Disinfect cutting tools with 10% bleach solution between plants
✓ Avoid overhead irrigation — bacteria spread via water splash
✗ DO NOT recommend fungicides — ineffective against bacteria

{% elif disease_category == "viral" %}
VIRAL DISEASE:
⚠ NO chemical cure exists for viral diseases
✓ Remove and destroy severely infected plants IMMEDIATELY
✓ Control insect vectors (aphids, whitefly, thrips) with appropriate insecticide
✓ Disinfect tools between plants to prevent mechanical transmission
✓ Source certified virus-free planting material for next season
✗ DO NOT recommend fungicides or bactericides for the virus itself

{% elif disease_category == "nutrient_deficiency" %}
NUTRIENT DEFICIENCY:
⚠ Pesticides will NOT help — this is a nutritional issue
✓ Check and correct soil pH first — most deficiencies are pH-related
✓ Apply the specific deficient nutrient — reference knowledge base for rates
✓ Consider foliar application for rapid correction
✓ Conduct soil testing to confirm before applying amendments
✗ DO NOT recommend any pesticide

{% elif disease_category == "abiotic_stress" %}
ABIOTIC STRESS:
⚠ Chemicals will NOT resolve environmental stress
✓ Address root cause: irrigation, drainage, shade, or soil compaction
✓ Apply mulch to regulate soil moisture and temperature
✓ Adjust irrigation timing to avoid waterlogging or drought stress
✗ DO NOT recommend any pesticide

{% elif disease_category == "insect" %}
INSECT / PEST:
✓ Scout field to confirm pest identity and infestation level first
✓ Apply neem oil (20ml/litre) for soft-bodied insects — safe and locally available
✓ Use locally approved insecticide for severe infestations — follow label guidance
✓ Remove and destroy heavily infested leaves to reduce pest load
✓ Introduce biological controls where available
✗ DO NOT recommend fungicides or bactericides for pest damage
{% endif %}

━━ QUALITY REQUIREMENTS ━━
✓ Give 5-6 treatments — mix of immediate, organic, chemical, and preventive types
✓ Be SPECIFIC — use product types, application rates, and timings from the knowledge base
✓ Reference Uganda/East Africa context — mention agrovets, extension officers, NARO
✓ Each treatment must be directly relevant to {{ diagnosis.name if diagnosis else "this disease" }}
✗ Do NOT give generic farming advice unrelated to this specific disease
✗ Do NOT repeat the same advice in different words

{% if personality == "friendly" %}
Use simple, encouraging language. Assume the farmer has basic tools and agrovet access.
Mention where to get products (local agrovet, extension officer, NARO).
{% elif personality == "formal" %}
Use precise technical terminology. Include application rates and timing where known.
{% elif personality == "concise" %}
Give exactly 5 treatments. One sentence per details field. Be direct.
{% endif %}

Respond ONLY with a valid JSON array. No markdown, no backticks, no extra text:

[
  {
    "type": "immediate | organic | chemical | preventive",
    "action": "specific short title (e.g. 'Apply Copper Oxychloride Fungicide')",
    "details": "Specific instructions referencing the knowledge base content — include product type, rate, timing, and safety note where relevant"
  }
]